  "title": "fix: preserve live Map iteration during draft mutations",
  "user": {
    "login": "Marve10s",
    "id": 126423069,
    "node_id": "U_kgDOB4kQHQ",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126423069?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Marve10s",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Marve10s/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "Mutating a draft Map during iteration can visit deleted entries and skip added entries when no earlier operation has created the draft's copy.\n\n```js\nconst seen = []\nproduce(new Map([[\"a\", 1], [\"b\", 2]]), draft => {\n  draft.forEach((value, key) => {\n    seen.push([key, value])\n    if (key === \"a\") {\n      draft.delete(\"b\")\n      draft.set(\"c\", 3)\n    }\n  })\n})\n```\n\nPreviously `seen` was `[[\"a\", 1], [\"b\", undefined]]`; it now matches native Map behavior: `[[\"a\", 1], [\"c\", 3]]`.\n\nPrepare the copy before `forEach` and `keys` start iterating, so iteration and subsequent mutations use the same backing Map. This also fixes `values`, `entries`, and `Symbol.iterator`, which use `keys`. Read-only iteration now creates a shallow copy, but an unmodified producer still returns the original state. The regression cases cover all five entry points in the existing configuration matrix.\n\nThis restores native live-iteration semantics: repeatedly deleting and re-adding the current key, or continually adding keys during traversal, can keep iteration running just as it would on a plain Map.\n",
